016)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 370 people. Revenue per employee of $1.4M ranks in the below the sector median among Energy peers. Stock-based compensation of $33K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["W&T Offshore, Inc. is a small-cap energy business with a $519M market cap on $501M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -18% over the past three years and -0% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 6% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin -1.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 35% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (-0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Energy peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 26% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (13.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 61/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"The commodity cycle \u2014 revenue and free cash flow are ultimately hostage to a price the company does not set, and the long-run energy-transition arc adds a structural overhang.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 44% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Energy sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Down 24.5% in 4 Weeks, Here's Why You Should You Buy the Dip in W&T (WTI)","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3028143/down-24-5-in-4-weeks-here-s-why-you-should-you-buy-the-dip-in-w-t-wti?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Crsi-3028143","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794428150.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"It Might Not Be A Great Idea To Buy W&T Offshore, Inc. (NYSE:WTI) For Its Next Dividend","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/energy/nyse-wti/wt-offshore/news/it-might-not-be-a-great-idea-to-buy-wt-offshore-inc-nysewti","date":"2026-11-08","timestamp":1794140900.529,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.201,"tier